    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "47e734cd_7b30476e",
        "filename": "tools/testrunners/common/android/adb_test.bzl",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 79,
      "author": {
        "id": 5395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-27T20:20:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would this be easier/better to do in the go program? I would like a simple shell scripts as possible, so could we have the go program remove the flag it cares about?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 79,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 79,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "b6896cb52de7b54d33c207ea5038beae34cc5e3d",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9ab23bf9_ae81b454",
        "filename": "tools/testrunners/common/android/adb_test.bzl",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 79,
      "author": {
        "id": 10009
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-27T21:21:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IIUC the alternative is to have `adb_test_runner.go` parse flag `--test-runner-extra-args` and extract `--device-specific-bazel-config \u003cconfig-name\u003e`. The remainder of `--test-runner-extra-args` would be passed to the underlying C++ binary, and `adb_test_runner.go` would use `\u003cconfig-name\u003e` as if it were its own flag.\n\nMy reasoning to do that parsing step here is that, from a semantic POV, it seemed cleaner than having a `--test-runner-extra-args` flag where some values are given special treatment. If we did the parsing step in Go, I thought the reader would have to carry the extra cognitive load of renaming `--test-runner-extra-args` to `--test-runner-extra-args-except-for-...` in their head.\n\nHaving said that, I\u0027ll defer to your preference because you are effectively the reader here. Happy to move this step into `adb_test_runner.go` if you think that\u0027s best.",
      "parentUuid": "47e734cd_7b30476e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 79,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 79,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "b6896cb52de7b54d33c207ea5038beae34cc5e3d",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a6fd9f18_b05ace56",
        "filename": "tools/testrunners/common/android/adb_test.bzl",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 79,
      "author": {
        "id": 5395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-27T21:29:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think having this sort of \"special casing\" logic live in go code is preferable (and more testable) than here in shell scripts.",
      "parentUuid": "9ab23bf9_ae81b454",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 79,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 79,
        "endChar": 38
      },
